  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{1}{7}$ on the left and $\\frac{5}{7}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129500/assets/16fba9ecbb17fc504413d656d8434c10b33f330e448ab9da24cd6105ad7251c6.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $1$ shaded piece, and the shape on the right has $5$ shaded pieces. So the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of $5.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{7}\\times 5=\\frac{5}{7}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $5.$",
